- actor(a_default, ...): The model assigns all nodes to a single default actor, ignoring the source text which explicitly assigns responsibilities to "Faculty" (for action(n4, ...): "Faculty will choose the design") and "MPC" (for action(n9, ...), action(n10, ...), and action(n13, ...): "MPC should Calculate...", "MPC should add...", "MPC should notify...").
- action(n1, "start"): This action is hallucinated as a separate step; the text specifies that "To start the process, Course Packet Information Received should be sent" (which corresponds to n2).
- action(n7, "is copyright cleared?") and action(n11, "is price finalized?"): These are modeled as standalone actions, but the text describes them as the conditional logic of the gateways themselves ("If there is a need...", "However, if...").
- branch(b1, XOR) and branch(b2, XOR): The model is missing `guard` statements on the outgoing edges of these branches to represent the explicit source conditions (e.g., "Entire Course Packet Copyright Cleared", "Price of the Course Packet is finalized").
- action(n8, ...) and action(n12, ...): Both of these nodes lack outgoing `precedence` edges, resulting in dead ends. The source text explicitly dictates for both branches that "the process should be continued", implying a progression or loop back.
- action(n13, "notify: Notify bookstore of finalization"): The payload omits mandatory details from the text, which states to "notify the Bookstore of the Course packet, Course number, Faculty name, and sections."
- action(n14, "end"): The model omits the final notification step described in the text: "Once the MPC notifies the Bookstore, the Packet information should be notified to the Bookstore", before the process ends.
- defines(v1, ...) and defines(v2, ...): The variable definitions have empty ranges `{}`, failing to define the valid value spaces for the condition outcomes.

Structural Check
- [S1] STC8 failed: Each action node must have exactly one incoming and one outgoing edge. | Node `n12` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n8` has in=1 and out=0. | DSL: action(n12,"reconsider: Re-evaluate content after reconsideration"); action(n8,"notify: Contact Faculty to inform of denial and ask if new content should be added")
- [S2] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v2` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S3] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n8` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n9` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n12` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n13` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.
- [S4] STC20 failed: Every non-end node must have a path to at least one end node. | Violations: n12, n8 | DSL: action(n12,"reconsider: Re-evaluate content after reconsideration"); action(n8,"notify: Contact Faculty to inform of denial and ask if new content should be added")